<<~ ahu slot=`#/contract`>>

!! TW5 Boot Gate — Contract

`bootTrustedModules(tw, preloaded, granted)` (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-module-gate.ts`) runs inside `TW5Engine.boot`, in the host boot callback. It adds JavaScript tiddlers from the ''live corpus'' (tiddlers the wiki holds from `preloadTiddlers`), after TW5 completes its own module collection — so execution of a gated body during that boot reads UNBUILT. When no corpus meme passes the gate it injects nothing; the gate carries no imperative fallback of its own.

```
bootTrustedModules(tw, preloaded, granted)
    │
    ├─ wiki.filterTiddlers([all[tiddlers]stack:has[MODULE_COMPONENT_URI]])
    │       │  for each matching tiddler:
    │       ├─ skip a title the genesis preload did not hold
    │       ├─ Layer 1: the title sits in the granted set (the promote ledger digest, hand-committed, not shadowed by kāpae) — otherwise refuse and warn
    │       ├─ skip an empty body
    │       ├─ Layer 2: tagged SHA-256(text) equals the source-sha256 field
    │       └─ Layer 3: module-type is library — any other type refuses by name
    │
    ├─ each pass → wiki.addTiddler({ type: application/javascript, module-type, text })
    │
    ├─ each pass → tw.modules.define(title, "library", text)
    │                  (TW5 reads a module by the name another module requires: its title)
    │
    └─ if none passed → nothing injects; the packed plugin's own module tiddlers
                        carry the parser, the deserializer and the widgets
```

''Why two paths?'' The corpus path names the target steady state: all logic lives as `lar:` memes, verified by hash and a local promote grant. The packed plugin keeps the app booting and working offline, on cold start, and before any meme passes every gate layer.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/thresholds`>>

!! Gate Conditions

No score gates execution. A carrier runs only when this device holds a local grant for it:

| Condition | Reading |
|---|---|
| preload | the title came in with the genesis preload, never joined after boot |
| grant | the title appears in the granted set, the promote ledger's hand-committed digest for that wiki, not shadowed by a kāpae revocation |
| digest | `source-sha256` verifies against the `text` field (integrity relative to the claim, never authenticity or consent) |
| type | `module-type` reads `library` |

Fail closed: a carrier missing any condition injects nothing. The promote lane's gate (`tw5-module-gate.ts` at the promote branch) retired the level parser; no field value on a carrier authorizes execution. A keyhive capability proof reads UNBUILT.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/stuck-in-ts`>>

!! Why No Meme Can Carry This

`bootTrustedModules` requires a live `$tw` reference to call `wiki.filterTiddlers()`, `wiki.addTiddler()`, and `tw.modules.define()` — runtime calls against the TW5 instance `boot()` creates. No wikitext expresses the gate logic and no tiddler loads it: the gate decides which memes become executable.

''The gate queries a COMPONENT, and a meme carries that component'': `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/tw5/tw5-module`. The gate asks `[stack:has[…]]` — which carriers WEAR it — never what kind a carrier claims. Any carrier wearing that component, holding a local grant and passing the content hash, gets injected by the corpus path.

The distinction makes the whole gate. ''Authority rides on what a carrier holds and who granted it, never on its kind'': a carrier cannot declare itself executable, it can only wear a component whose own meme states what wearing it costs, and the stack entry carries no verb of its own.

<<~/ahu>>

